---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  description="Terms for using the Woodfox Coffee Company website."
  updated="October 14, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to your use of woodfoxcoffee.com, operated by {site.legalName} of {site.location}. By using the
    site you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2>About this website</h2>
  <p>
    This website provides information about Woodfox Coffee, our coffees, our approach and our wholesale programme.
    <strong>Online ordering is not currently available</strong>, and no purchases can be made through the site. Coffees
    shown as placeholders or “coming soon” are not offers for sale.
  </p>
  <p>
    When online ordering launches, additional terms covering orders, pricing, payment, subscriptions, shipping and
    returns will apply, and this page will be updated.
  </p>

  <h2>Product information</h2>
  <p>
    We work to describe our coffees accurately. Tasting notes describe flavour characteristics we perceive when cupping;
    no flavourings are added. Details may change between harvests and roasts.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The Woodfox name, logo, text and original media on this site belong to {site.legalName} and may not be used without
    permission. Some photographs are licensed from third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Please don’t misuse the site, including by attempting to disrupt it, gain unauthorised access, or send spam through
    our forms.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>We may link to other websites. We are not responsible for their content or practices.</p>

  <h2>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided “as is.” To the extent permitted by law, {site.legalName} is not liable for indirect or
    consequential losses arising from your use of the site.
    <mark class="confirm">[owner and counsel to review wording]</mark>
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas
    <mark class="confirm">[owner and counsel to confirm venue, e.g. Harris County]</mark>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
